Hey, to be fair, the other teams were filled with special business actors, okay?

1283
00:56:27.350 --> 00:56:32.550
So after I listened to the DVD commentary, I thought, oh, I've got to watch Scranton and Utica play.

1284
00:56:32.930 --> 00:56:35.550
Ken said that Utica crushed you guys.

1285
00:56:35.670 --> 00:56:39.090
So I went back and watched the episode and I never saw you guys play Utica.

1286
00:56:39.230 --> 00:56:40.610
It's in the deleted scenes.

1287
00:56:40.610 --> 00:56:41.730
Oh, wow.

1288
00:56:42.030 --> 00:56:42.250
Yeah.

1289
00:56:42.410 --> 00:56:45.510
And it features some major trash talking Andy.

1290
00:56:46.590 --> 00:56:47.490
Send it back.

1291
00:56:47.750 --> 00:56:48.090
Yeah.

1292
00:56:48.330 --> 00:56:49.350
Send that ball back.

1293
00:56:50.530 --> 00:56:52.070
Don't mess with Scranton.

1294
00:56:52.270 --> 00:56:52.470
No.

1295
00:56:52.630 --> 00:56:52.950
Uh-uh.

1296
00:56:53.270 --> 00:56:53.710
Utica.

1297
00:56:54.030 --> 00:56:55.310
More like you sucks to cuff.

1298
00:56:55.630 --> 00:56:56.470
Who sucks to cuff?

1299
00:56:56.670 --> 00:56:57.570
You sucks to cuff.

1300
00:56:57.710 --> 00:56:58.630
Who sucks to cuff?

1301
00:56:58.730 --> 00:56:59.690
You sucks to cuff.

1302
00:56:59.870 --> 00:57:00.690
Who sucks to cuff?

1303
00:57:00.830 --> 00:57:01.750
You sucks to cuff.

1304
00:57:01.890 --> 00:57:02.090
Ow.

1305
00:57:02.270 --> 00:57:02.430
Ow.

1306
00:57:03.170 --> 00:57:03.610
Sorry.

1307
00:57:05.210 --> 00:57:09.330
Jim comes up to Andy and Dwight and he's like pinching their arms so they stop.

1308
00:57:09.330 --> 00:57:13.310
But yeah, Andy starts this whole chant about you sucks to cuff.

1309
00:57:13.690 --> 00:57:14.910
Oh, my gosh.

1310
00:57:15.110 --> 00:57:17.490
But in reality, they were crushing us.

1311
00:57:17.590 --> 00:57:17.750
Yeah.

1312
00:57:18.730 --> 00:57:19.790
Oh, I love that.

1313
00:57:20.390 --> 00:57:22.850
Radit, dad, dad, don't mess with Scranton.

1314
00:57:23.290 --> 00:57:24.870
That made me laugh so hard.

1315
00:57:25.630 --> 00:57:29.310
It's time for Michael and Holly's presentation.

1316
00:57:30.110 --> 00:57:31.010
Oh, gosh.

1317
00:57:31.670 --> 00:57:33.850
This is when David says, I have not seen this.

1318
00:57:34.850 --> 00:57:38.230
He announces that they're going to sing a song, and they're like, no, no, no, it's a sketch.

1319
00:57:38.490 --> 00:57:39.290
No, it's a sketch.

1320
00:57:39.830 --> 00:57:42.630
They're like, David, you should already be worried.

1321
00:57:42.870 --> 00:57:43.090
Yeah.

1322
00:57:43.330 --> 00:57:47.210
And then they say, introducing Slumdunder Mifflinair.

1323
00:57:47.910 --> 00:57:52.250
So Slumdog Millionaire was a hit movie that came out in 2008.

1324
00:57:52.870 --> 00:57:58.570
According to IMDb, and this is a very brief synopsis, this is what it says.

1325
00:57:58.890 --> 00:58:06.310
A Mumbai teenager reflects on his life after being accused of cheating on the Indian version of Who Wants to Be a Millionaire?

1326
00:58:06.870 --> 00:58:08.030
Well, I saw this movie.

1327
00:58:08.110 --> 00:58:08.730
It was fantastic.

1328
00:58:08.830 --> 00:58:09.690
Oh, it's so good.

1329
00:58:09.770 --> 00:58:10.250
It's so good.

1330
00:58:10.410 --> 00:58:11.670
Everyone was talking about it.

1331
00:58:11.710 --> 00:58:13.810
Yes, it was huge and just a great film.

1332
00:58:13.970 --> 00:58:19.130
It won a gazillion of awards, including the Academy Award for Best Picture in 2009.

1333
00:58:19.130 --> 00:58:28.570
But of all the movies to parody, to tell the story of Robert Dunder and Robert Mifflin coming together, no one knows what they're doing.

1334
00:58:28.970 --> 00:58:31.810
Well, they're also going to get some facts wrong.

1335
00:58:32.450 --> 00:58:35.230
Fan catch from KCK in Orlando, Florida.

1336
00:58:35.630 --> 00:58:40.750
In Michael and Holly's sketch, they say that Dunder and Mifflin met in college.

1337
00:58:40.910 --> 00:58:43.830
At Dartmouth, which incidentally is where Mindy went.

1338
00:58:43.830 --> 00:58:49.790
But in Dunder Mifflin Infinity, Robert Mifflin said he knew Dunder through the Rotary Club.

1339
00:58:50.050 --> 00:58:50.510
Mm-hmm.

1340
00:58:50.970 --> 00:58:51.390
Mm-hmm.

1341
00:58:51.630 --> 00:58:52.030
So.

1342
00:58:52.210 --> 00:58:53.110
I caught it, too.

1343
00:58:53.450 --> 00:58:53.650
Yeah.

1344
00:58:54.190 --> 00:59:02.330
Ken shared that they really just drove home with the crowd watching to please not react in any way.

1345
00:59:02.690 --> 00:59:03.850
Even the children.

1346
00:59:04.110 --> 00:59:05.370
Don't crack a smile.

1347
00:59:05.670 --> 00:59:06.150
Nothing.

1348
00:59:06.470 --> 00:59:06.810
Mm-hmm.

1349
00:59:06.810 --> 00:59:14.210
And Ken was so happy with how the scene turned out, because everyone really just looks at them so deadpan.

1350
00:59:14.730 --> 00:59:20.890
And Ken said that Steve and Amy pulled him aside after the first take, and they were like, this feels really uncomfortable.

1351
00:59:21.410 --> 00:59:23.090
This is, like, so awkward.

1352
00:59:23.310 --> 00:59:25.550
Amy was like, I'm rattled by it.

1353
00:59:25.930 --> 00:59:29.790
Because it truly felt like they were bombing on stage in front of everyone.

1354
00:59:29.790 --> 00:59:42.210
Well, I guess this sketch took, like, hours to shoot, and in addition to being told not to laugh, the extras were not allowed to move from their spots for continuity reasons.

1355
00:59:42.210 --> 00:59:47.130
So we would bring Waters around and things like that, but they had to stay right there.

1356
00:59:47.350 --> 00:59:52.030
And Jenny Tan had this tidbit in her breakdown from her visit.

1357
00:59:52.030 --> 01:00:02.570
But Andy Buckley, who plays David Wallace, would get on the little stage during the breaks, and he would entertain the crowd with stories and jokes.

1358
01:00:02.630 --> 01:00:04.350
She said he even sang a song.

1359
01:00:04.610 --> 01:00:05.610
Oh, my gosh.

1360
01:00:05.730 --> 01:00:07.490
But he was like the entertainment.

1361
01:00:07.890 --> 01:00:11.690
And she said it was just like the sweetest, most thoughtful thing.

1362
01:00:11.910 --> 01:00:12.690
And you know what?

1363
01:00:12.770 --> 01:00:14.570
That is Andy Buckley right there.

1364
01:00:14.670 --> 01:00:14.950
Yeah.

1365
01:00:15.110 --> 01:00:16.910
I was like, of course he did that.

1366
01:00:16.990 --> 01:00:17.530
Of course.

1367
01:00:17.750 --> 01:00:18.790
That is so sweet.

1368
01:00:19.010 --> 01:00:19.210
Yeah.

1369
01:00:19.210 --> 01:00:22.110
Well, the only person that's enjoying this is Stanley.

1370
01:00:22.430 --> 01:00:29.610
We have some classic vacation Stanley when he has his cocktail, and he says, I usually don't enjoy the theater, but this is delightful.

1371
01:00:30.010 --> 01:00:32.170
I think he's had a few cocktails by this point.

1372
01:00:32.350 --> 01:00:33.250
I guess he has.

1373
01:00:33.490 --> 01:00:36.330
There's a lot of booze being offered at this event.

1374
01:00:38.050 --> 01:00:40.510
Now Michael and Holly are going to do something.

1375
01:00:40.830 --> 01:00:44.410
They're going to announce that the Buffalo Branch is closing.

1376
01:00:44.870 --> 01:00:46.130
And then they take a bow.

1377
01:00:46.650 --> 01:00:48.570
This is news to the Buffalo Branch.

1378
01:00:48.570 --> 01:00:50.430
They are ticked off.

1379
01:00:50.690 --> 01:00:54.610
Well, there are two especially very angry Buffalo Branch employees.

1380
01:00:54.970 --> 01:00:59.270
They were played by Brian Stack and Marla Garland.

1381
01:00:59.510 --> 01:01:03.170
Brian Stack was a writer on Conan, and I've known Marla for years.

1382
01:01:03.350 --> 01:01:04.530
She is just delightful.

1383
01:01:04.930 --> 01:01:09.930
Well, also seated in the front row, who's very upset about this branch closing, is Jenny Tan.

1384
01:01:10.270 --> 01:01:10.830
Yes.

1385
01:01:10.830 --> 01:01:22.590
And she revealed that she was in the front row with a real-life husband and wife couple, Dan and Aaron, who were booked together to play extras on this episode.

1386
01:01:22.590 --> 01:01:24.290
They gave them two fake babies.

1387
01:01:24.390 --> 01:01:26.010
And it's really great.

1388
01:01:26.010 --> 01:01:29.070
You can see Dan sitting next to Jenny.

1389
01:01:29.090 --> 01:01:35.090
And when Brian Stack, as the angry Buffalo Man, is yelling, he's shushing his baby.

1390
01:01:35.210 --> 01:01:37.390
He's like, shh, shh, shh, shh, shh, shh.

1391
01:01:37.410 --> 01:01:39.350
Don't let the angry man upset you, baby.

1392
01:01:39.350 --> 01:01:41.030
Yes, exactly, exactly.

1393
01:01:42.370 --> 01:01:44.310
David Wallace is furious.

1394
01:01:44.690 --> 01:01:47.830
This is not how he wanted the Buffalo Branch to find out.

1395
01:01:48.070 --> 01:01:48.450
No.

1396
01:01:48.630 --> 01:01:52.650
He says one little boy just asked him if Daddy will have his job at Christmas.

1397
01:01:53.070 --> 01:01:56.190
And Michael's like, well, he's just thinking about his own gifts.

1398
01:01:56.310 --> 01:01:57.290
Not helping, Michael.

1399
01:01:58.670 --> 01:02:00.730
The Scranton group huddles up.

1400
01:02:00.830 --> 01:02:02.110
They're over by the picnic tables.

1401
01:02:02.310 --> 01:02:05.430
And Meredith is like, I think we should forfeit the game out of respect.

1402
01:02:05.430 --> 01:02:09.090
And Dwight says people need volleyball now more than ever.

1403
01:02:09.670 --> 01:02:11.050
Oscar agrees with Dwight.

1404
01:02:11.290 --> 01:02:12.610
Now they have this rallying call.

1405
01:02:12.710 --> 01:02:14.170
They want to kick corporate's ass.

1406
01:02:14.570 --> 01:02:14.810
Yeah.

1407
01:02:14.970 --> 01:02:16.230
And they're doing great.

1408
01:02:16.650 --> 01:02:19.990
Especially Jim, which we get a little bit of.

1409
01:02:20.090 --> 01:02:20.730
Petty Charles.

1410
01:02:21.010 --> 01:02:21.350
Yes.

1411
01:02:21.510 --> 01:02:22.090
Petty Charles.

1412
01:02:22.170 --> 01:02:22.630
Thank you.

1413
01:02:22.830 --> 01:02:25.210
Petty Charles says, look who just woke up.

1414
01:02:25.270 --> 01:02:28.070
And then scores a point and says, I've been up for a while.

1415
01:02:28.410 --> 01:02:28.850
Okay.

1416
01:02:28.990 --> 01:02:32.170
So now Dwight is going to stand up to Rolf.

1417
01:02:32.610 --> 01:02:33.430
He is.

1418
01:02:33.430 --> 01:02:39.270
And Jenna, I had one of those moments where I think I thought I heard something that's

1419
01:02:39.270 --> 01:02:40.090
not in the script.

1420
01:02:40.630 --> 01:02:42.030
It's not in the subtitles.

1421
01:02:42.190 --> 01:02:44.090
And I need you to tell me what I heard.

1422
01:02:44.410 --> 01:02:44.570
What?

1423
01:02:44.930 --> 01:02:46.030
Yeah, exactly.

1424
01:02:46.510 --> 01:02:48.250
Kevin says, it's six to six.

1425
01:02:48.390 --> 01:02:49.210
It's a nail biter.

1426
01:02:49.610 --> 01:02:51.450
Angela says, Kevin, no, it's seven, six.

1427
01:02:51.570 --> 01:02:53.130
Or is that too much accounting for you?

1428
01:02:53.690 --> 01:02:55.830
Rolf says, here's an accounting question for you.

1429
01:02:55.990 --> 01:02:58.510
What does one fiance plus one lover equal?

1430
01:02:58.890 --> 01:03:00.170
Answer, one whore.

1431
01:03:00.590 --> 01:03:02.870
Dwight says, okay, knock it off, Rolf.

1432
01:03:03.450 --> 01:03:04.170
Rolf says, what?

1433
01:03:04.370 --> 01:03:06.690
She is sitting here casting aspirations.

1434
01:03:07.090 --> 01:03:08.910
And Dwight goes, Rolfard, please.

1435
01:03:09.610 --> 01:03:13.630
Jenna, I swear I hear Dwight say Rolfard, please.

1436
01:03:14.270 --> 01:03:17.130
Meaning like Rolfard is Rolf's full name?

1437
01:03:17.350 --> 01:03:17.870
Yes.

1438
01:03:18.490 --> 01:03:20.070
It's not documented anywhere.

1439
01:03:20.070 --> 01:03:21.510
I'm probably just losing it.

1440
01:03:21.690 --> 01:03:22.770
I need you to hear it.

1441
01:03:22.870 --> 01:03:23.490
I'm going to play it.

1442
01:03:23.710 --> 01:03:23.890
Ready?

1443
01:03:24.170 --> 01:03:24.430
Okay.

1444
01:03:30.270 --> 01:03:31.370
Oh, okay.

1445
01:03:32.070 --> 01:03:33.010
Rolfard, please.

1446
01:03:33.010 --> 01:03:34.050
I'm telling you.

1447
01:03:34.050 --> 01:03:36.850
Okay, here's the first thing I need to know is this.

1448
01:03:37.030 --> 01:03:38.070
Is Rolf a name?

1449
01:03:38.350 --> 01:03:39.250
That I don't know.

1450
01:03:39.330 --> 01:03:41.150
Did we make that up or is it a name?

1451
01:03:41.650 --> 01:03:43.370
Is Rolf short for Rolfard?

1452
01:03:44.130 --> 01:03:47.090
Well, there's a restaurant in Manhattan called Rolf's.

1453
01:03:47.410 --> 01:03:48.770
It's in Gramercy Park.

1454
01:03:49.850 --> 01:03:51.110
Oh, here we go.

1455
01:03:51.230 --> 01:03:51.710
Wikipedia.

1456
01:03:52.330 --> 01:03:52.810
Rolf.

1457
01:03:53.050 --> 01:03:55.310
It is a male given name and surname.

1458
01:03:55.310 --> 01:03:59.350
It originates in the Germanic name Rolf.

1459
01:03:59.970 --> 01:04:00.670
Interesting.

1460
01:04:01.130 --> 01:04:03.090
But now Rolfard.

1461
01:04:03.970 --> 01:04:04.750
Rolfard.

1462
01:04:05.770 --> 01:04:08.710
We need background music for ladies who Google.

1463
01:04:08.990 --> 01:04:09.750
Like Jeopardy.

1464
01:04:09.810 --> 01:04:09.970
We really do.

1465
01:04:11.170 --> 01:04:16.790
Okay, I will tell you there is the Rolfard Leather Company in the UK.

1466
01:04:16.790 --> 01:04:19.490
They are a supplier of fine quality leathers.

1467
01:04:19.490 --> 01:04:26.770
Also, just from Ancestry.com, Michigan had the highest population of Rolfard families in 1880.

1468
01:04:26.970 --> 01:04:29.410
So, I think you might be right.

1469
01:04:29.730 --> 01:04:31.470
Both names seem to be names.

1470
01:04:31.710 --> 01:04:32.790
I mean, just come on.

1471
01:04:33.070 --> 01:04:38.070
I think you're right.

1472
01:04:38.390 --> 01:04:41.130
I think we have broken a big case here.

1473
01:04:41.490 --> 01:04:44.150
Mom detectives, we declare Rolfard.

1474
01:04:44.350 --> 01:04:48.930
Put it on your calendar that this is the first time Rolfard is being documented?

1475
01:04:49.270 --> 01:04:49.630
Yes.

1476
01:04:50.150 --> 01:04:51.670
In the office canon.

1477
01:04:52.430 --> 01:04:53.070
Angela.

1478
01:04:53.070 --> 01:04:53.970
I'm clapping for myself.

1479
01:04:54.270 --> 01:04:54.830
Applause for you.

1480
01:04:55.190 --> 01:04:55.670
Thank you.

1481
01:04:55.850 --> 01:04:56.650
Good work.

1482
01:04:56.850 --> 01:04:57.230
Thank you.

1483
01:04:57.390 --> 01:04:59.450
And now to whoever does subtitles, change it to Rolfard.

1484
01:04:59.530 --> 01:05:00.150
Thank you very much.

1485
01:05:00.290 --> 01:05:05.230
I'd like to say that that was a combo mom detective to ladies who Google move.

1486
01:05:05.430 --> 01:05:08.150
Do you see how both of those came together?

1487
01:05:08.830 --> 01:05:09.910
It's beautiful, really.

1488
01:05:10.050 --> 01:05:10.630
In that moment.

1489
01:05:10.770 --> 01:05:11.090
I do.

1490
01:05:11.250 --> 01:05:11.950
I'm proud of us.

1491
01:05:12.730 --> 01:05:16.710
Ken shared that he really liked seeing Dwight softening to Angela.

1492
01:05:17.610 --> 01:05:19.290
Angela's clearly moved by this.

1493
01:05:19.290 --> 01:05:23.090
And then, right after the scene, there would have been an Angela talking head.

1494
01:05:23.270 --> 01:05:25.250
It got deleted, but I wanted you to hear it.

1495
01:05:26.050 --> 01:05:29.430
Today, for the first time in months, Dwight nodded at me.

1496
01:05:30.170 --> 01:05:34.810
And I have to admit, it made my heart sit up just a little straighter in its chair.

1497
01:05:35.210 --> 01:05:40.590
I know I seem hard and cold on the outside, but on the inside, I'm as warm as porcelain.

1498
01:05:40.590 --> 01:05:44.580
And I'm sorry for gushing on like this.

1499
01:05:45.960 --> 01:05:48.980
It just must be the apple juice talking or...

1500
01:05:48.980 --> 01:05:49.960
I don't...

1501
01:05:51.880 --> 01:05:52.960
It's very sweet.

1502
01:05:53.560 --> 01:05:56.480
She is as soft as porcelain on the inside.

1503
01:05:57.400 --> 01:05:59.320
Apple juice is not on the drink menu.

1504
01:05:59.320 --> 01:06:00.560
I knew you were going to say that.

1505
01:06:00.820 --> 01:06:03.200
I also now like this expression of saying,

1506
01:06:03.340 --> 01:06:06.240
it just made my heart sit up a little straighter in its chair.

1507
01:06:06.240 --> 01:06:07.220
I loved that too.

1508
01:06:07.220 --> 01:06:08.420
I thought it was cute.

1509
01:06:09.380 --> 01:06:13.740
The game is going and Pam is going to fall.

1510
01:06:14.400 --> 01:06:16.120
Lady, I did my own falling stunt.

1511
01:06:16.280 --> 01:06:16.780
That's all me.

1512
01:06:17.020 --> 01:06:17.980
I believed it.

1513
01:06:18.060 --> 01:06:18.900
I'm very proud of it.

1514
01:06:19.080 --> 01:06:21.520
It's not the first time you fall in this episode.

1515
01:06:21.520 --> 01:06:22.520
You fall twice.

1516
01:06:22.720 --> 01:06:23.220
I do?

1517
01:06:23.440 --> 01:06:23.600
Yeah.

1518
01:06:23.840 --> 01:06:29.780
You had a spontaneous fall while you were playing fake volleyball earlier in the episode.

1519
01:06:29.960 --> 01:06:30.300
Oh.

1520
01:06:30.460 --> 01:06:31.260
I clocked it.

1521
01:06:31.360 --> 01:06:33.220
You went down to your knees to get a ball.

1522
01:06:33.620 --> 01:06:33.980
Huh.

1523
01:06:34.240 --> 01:06:34.540
Mm-hmm.

1524
01:06:34.920 --> 01:06:35.700
I'm a pro.

1525
01:06:35.920 --> 01:06:37.260
You are sporty, Pam.

1526
01:06:38.000 --> 01:06:40.680
Well, there had been a lot of discussion about using my double

1527
01:06:40.680 --> 01:06:43.080
and shooting the fall from behind.

1528
01:06:43.480 --> 01:06:47.460
But Ken said to sell it, they really needed to see my face on camera.

1529
01:06:47.640 --> 01:06:49.360
And it wasn't the shoulder rotation.

1530
01:06:49.800 --> 01:06:50.320
Yes.

1531
01:06:50.400 --> 01:06:52.820
There was no reason why they couldn't just have me fall.

1532
01:06:53.000 --> 01:06:54.740
It was not going to affect my shoulder.

1533
01:06:55.480 --> 01:06:57.980
Randy told me that sometimes in movies,

1534
01:06:57.980 --> 01:07:01.760
they will use a stunt double from the front,

1535
01:07:01.760 --> 01:07:04.720
and then they do CGI face replacement.

1536
01:07:05.020 --> 01:07:05.380
What?

1537
01:07:05.600 --> 01:07:05.800
Yeah.

1538
01:07:06.240 --> 01:07:07.100
Is this face off?

1539
01:07:07.100 --> 01:07:10.460
Kind of, like the movie magic version of face off.

1540
01:07:10.720 --> 01:07:12.400
He said, we could not afford that.

1541
01:07:12.800 --> 01:07:16.140
So there was no putting my face on her face.

1542
01:07:16.540 --> 01:07:16.840
Okay.

1543
01:07:17.300 --> 01:07:18.660
So you know, at the end of this,

1544
01:07:18.840 --> 01:07:22.720
when Pam is going to leave to get her ankle checked,

1545
01:07:23.420 --> 01:07:25.340
Dwight has to start stalling for time.

1546
01:07:25.540 --> 01:07:27.040
And the first thing he does is he, like,

1547
01:07:27.140 --> 01:07:29.160
kicks the volleyball really far away.

1548
01:07:29.160 --> 01:07:33.440
This reminded me of, like, the butthole kid growing up,

1549
01:07:33.540 --> 01:07:34.700
like when you played kickball,

1550
01:07:34.860 --> 01:07:37.300
who would have a tantrum and kick the ball real far.

1551
01:07:37.440 --> 01:07:37.780
Totally.

1552
01:07:38.020 --> 01:07:38.880
And someone had to go get it.

1553
01:07:39.040 --> 01:07:41.300
Well, we had a fan catch from Emily H.

1554
01:07:41.400 --> 01:07:43.060
in Ohio who said,

1555
01:07:43.060 --> 01:07:46.860
I have a background catch at 16 minutes, 55 seconds.

1556
01:07:47.140 --> 01:07:50.400
When Dwight kicks the volleyball away to stall the game,

1557
01:07:50.560 --> 01:07:55.120
there are some weird face cutout board picture things in the background,

1558
01:07:55.120 --> 01:07:59.120
and I think there is a person sticking their head through one of them.

1559
01:07:59.440 --> 01:07:59.660
Really?

1560
01:07:59.980 --> 01:08:01.200
I saw those things.

1561
01:08:01.200 --> 01:08:02.760
They look like something from a carnival.

1562
01:08:03.140 --> 01:08:03.640
All right.

1563
01:08:03.840 --> 01:08:05.700
I don't know if this is related,

1564
01:08:06.020 --> 01:08:10.180
but Jenny Tan wrote this in her diary for the day.

1565
01:08:10.600 --> 01:08:11.300
She said,

1566
01:08:11.400 --> 01:08:14.320
During the first few takes of Dwight kicking the ball,

1567
01:08:14.480 --> 01:08:17.680
there was a background performer hiding in the shack.

1568
01:08:18.680 --> 01:08:21.620
And whenever the volleyball was kicked near it,

1569
01:08:21.720 --> 01:08:25.940
this person would wave his arm outside the shack and ruin the take.

1570
01:08:26.480 --> 01:08:27.100
She said,

1571
01:08:27.180 --> 01:08:27.960
Needless to say,

1572
01:08:28.040 --> 01:08:29.980
this person was asked to leave the set

1573
01:08:29.980 --> 01:08:32.520
and was told not to return for the rest of the week.

1574
01:08:32.940 --> 01:08:33.700
I don't know.

1575
01:08:33.780 --> 01:08:34.580
What's happening?

1576
01:08:34.580 --> 01:08:35.380
I don't know.

1577
01:08:35.660 --> 01:08:36.400
I was like,

1578
01:08:36.480 --> 01:08:40.040
could that be the person whose face was in the little, like, picture?

1579
01:08:40.180 --> 01:08:42.160
Well, you know I'm going to go back and look.

1580
01:08:42.340 --> 01:08:42.700
I know.

1581
01:08:43.540 --> 01:08:45.240
Well, not in the shack,

1582
01:08:45.400 --> 01:08:46.260
waving their arms,

1583
01:08:46.320 --> 01:08:47.020
or Michael and Holly.

1584
01:08:47.140 --> 01:08:48.100
How's that for a transition?

1585
01:08:48.100 --> 01:08:49.380
That was a wonderful transition.

1586
01:08:49.380 --> 01:08:50.200
I like that.

1587
01:08:50.520 --> 01:08:51.620
We should share with you guys,

1588
01:08:51.620 --> 01:08:53.140
we often wonder how to transition.

1589
01:08:54.440 --> 01:08:58.340
We are trying so hard not to have every transition be lady.

1590
01:08:58.640 --> 01:08:59.720
Lady, our well.

1591
01:09:00.200 --> 01:09:00.600
Yes.

1592
01:09:00.760 --> 01:09:01.440
Oh, the wells.

1593
01:09:01.620 --> 01:09:01.980
The wells.

1594
01:09:02.120 --> 01:09:02.780
We do a lot of wells.

1595
01:09:03.060 --> 01:09:03.740
Dr. Peter Thibodeau,

1596
01:09:03.860 --> 01:09:05.040
please don't count the wells.

1597
01:09:05.140 --> 01:09:05.660
Oh, don't.

1598
01:09:05.820 --> 01:09:08.220
Oh, I have Dr. Thibodeau a few times,

1599
01:09:08.260 --> 01:09:09.200
and it was staggering.

1600
01:09:09.860 --> 01:09:10.380
Anyways,

1601
01:09:11.200 --> 01:09:14.620
Michael and Holly are going to reflect on their skit,

1602
01:09:14.620 --> 01:09:18.140
and on their mistake of mentioning the buffalo thing,

1603
01:09:18.760 --> 01:09:22.240
and they have this very sweet couplet of dialogue.

1604
01:09:22.440 --> 01:09:22.800
Mm-hmm.

1605
01:09:23.340 --> 01:09:24.100
Holly says,

1606
01:09:24.240 --> 01:09:25.460
well, I'm glad we did it.

1607
01:09:25.920 --> 01:09:26.700
Michael says,

1608
01:09:26.800 --> 01:09:27.120
me too.

1609
01:09:27.520 --> 01:09:29.020
And there's a long pause,

1610
01:09:29.040 --> 01:09:30.140
and he says,

1611
01:09:30.380 --> 01:09:33.120
we have a lot of good material for next year's sketch.

1612
01:09:33.600 --> 01:09:35.660
And she lights up and says,

1613
01:09:36.040 --> 01:09:36.780
I can't wait.

1614
01:09:36.780 --> 01:09:37.500
Mm-hmm.

1615
01:09:37.980 --> 01:09:41.240
Well, this was a really beautiful performance by Steve and Amy.

1616
01:09:41.620 --> 01:09:45.360
They shared in the DVD that everyone at Video Village,

1617
01:09:45.360 --> 01:09:47.280
where they were watching the playback, was crying.

1618
01:09:47.860 --> 01:09:50.060
They said Jenny was there, Jenny Tan.

1619
01:09:50.260 --> 01:09:50.900
She was crying.

1620
01:09:51.560 --> 01:09:56.940
And then Ken said something I just loved about this scene between Steve and Amy.

1621
01:09:57.060 --> 01:09:59.800
I wrote it down verbatim, and I want to read it to you.

1622
01:10:00.020 --> 01:10:00.200
Okay.

1623
01:10:00.720 --> 01:10:01.640
Ken said,

1624
01:10:02.240 --> 01:10:03.340
it's the toughest kind of scene,

1625
01:10:03.520 --> 01:10:04.080
because in a way,

1626
01:10:04.240 --> 01:10:05.040
everything is happening,

1627
01:10:05.200 --> 01:10:07.440
and nothing is happening all at once.

1628
01:10:07.940 --> 01:10:10.580
There's a gigantic shift that takes place,

1629
01:10:10.780 --> 01:10:12.080
but it's all under the surface,

1630
01:10:12.080 --> 01:10:16.560
and the challenge is to find it over and over again,

1631
01:10:17.080 --> 01:10:18.100
take after take,

1632
01:10:18.240 --> 01:10:19.880
as if they've never been there.

1633
01:10:20.400 --> 01:10:20.820
Mm-hmm.

1634
01:10:21.480 --> 01:10:21.860
Yeah.

1635
01:10:22.060 --> 01:10:23.680
I just thought that was really well said,

1636
01:10:23.680 --> 01:10:25.480
because every time they did it,

1637
01:10:25.560 --> 01:10:26.820
they had to have that discovery

1638
01:10:27.300 --> 01:10:30.920
of knowing that something just changed for both of them.

1639
01:10:31.320 --> 01:10:32.420
It's a beautiful scene.

1640
01:10:32.560 --> 01:10:32.820
Mm-hmm.

1641
01:10:33.160 --> 01:10:34.320
And then they say goodbye,

1642
01:10:34.780 --> 01:10:36.960
and then Michael has this fantastic talking head

1643
01:10:36.960 --> 01:10:40.260
where he says he didn't find the perfect moment that day

1644
01:10:40.260 --> 01:10:41.360
to share those things with her,

1645
01:10:41.420 --> 01:10:42.120
but it's okay,

1646
01:10:42.120 --> 01:10:43.600
because they're going to be one of those couples

1647
01:10:43.600 --> 01:10:44.920
who have a long story,

1648
01:10:45.160 --> 01:10:47.160
and he's just going to be patient.

1649
01:10:47.560 --> 01:10:47.940
Yeah.

1650
01:10:48.160 --> 01:10:49.240
Jen said in an interview

1651
01:10:49.240 --> 01:10:51.320
that they loved setting up this idea

1652
01:10:51.320 --> 01:10:54.280
that Michael was going to find a way at this picnic

1653
01:10:54.280 --> 01:10:56.320
to try to make his move with Holly.

1654
01:10:56.600 --> 01:10:59.300
But then, over the course of the day,

1655
01:10:59.500 --> 01:11:00.880
as he spent time with her,

1656
01:11:01.140 --> 01:11:04.260
he was reminded that they have something really special,

1657
01:11:04.800 --> 01:11:07.020
and he gains this more mature way

1658
01:11:07.020 --> 01:11:08.360
of looking at the relationship,

1659
01:11:08.840 --> 01:11:11.740
and it's very different than how he would behave

1660
01:11:11.740 --> 01:11:15.100
if this were Jan or any other woman from his past,

1661
01:11:15.620 --> 01:11:17.800
and that she said, quote,

1662
01:11:17.800 --> 01:11:22.360
he was calm and confident and quieted by this thought.

1663
01:11:22.950 --> 01:11:24.160
And I loved that.

1664
01:11:24.360 --> 01:11:24.740
Mm-hmm.

1665
01:11:24.880 --> 01:11:28.360
And this talking head right here

1666
01:11:28.360 --> 01:11:31.320
is why you know this is his soup snake.

1667
01:11:31.720 --> 01:11:32.360
Yeah.

1668
01:11:32.660 --> 01:11:33.580
His soulmate.

1669
01:11:34.980 --> 01:11:36.700
A hundred percent, right?

1670
01:11:37.200 --> 01:11:37.640
Yeah.

1671
01:11:37.980 --> 01:11:42.200
Well, Jim is going to take Pam to a local hospital,

1672
01:11:42.200 --> 01:11:44.820
and for whatever reason,

1673
01:11:44.820 --> 01:11:48.820
they have this belief that Dwight can stall this volleyball game.

1674
01:11:49.000 --> 01:11:49.740
I mean...

1675
01:11:49.740 --> 01:11:50.540
For how long?

1676
01:11:50.580 --> 01:11:51.400
I mean, you...

1677
01:11:51.400 --> 01:11:54.140
Have you ever gone to get an ankle checked

1678
01:11:54.140 --> 01:11:55.120
or anything checked?

1679
01:11:55.720 --> 01:11:57.880
Even just the commute and finding parking

1680
01:11:57.880 --> 01:11:59.760
and getting inside and signing up

1681
01:11:59.760 --> 01:12:02.320
and getting your insurance information and...

1682
01:12:02.320 --> 01:12:03.000
I don't know.

1683
01:12:03.340 --> 01:12:06.240
Jim is feverishly filling out some hospital form

1684
01:12:06.240 --> 01:12:09.420
while a sassy nurse is wheeling Pam away.

1685
01:12:10.140 --> 01:12:12.380
The sassy nurse was played by Allison Martin.

1686
01:12:12.380 --> 01:12:15.000
She's done a ton of television comedy,

1687
01:12:15.220 --> 01:12:16.580
most recently Grace and Frankie,

1688
01:12:16.820 --> 01:12:18.680
and she did an episode of Law & Order.

1689
01:12:19.000 --> 01:12:19.260
Oh.

1690
01:12:19.600 --> 01:12:21.660
We had a fan question from Christy H.

1691
01:12:21.740 --> 01:12:22.180
in Maryland,

1692
01:12:22.180 --> 01:12:22.780
who said,

1693
01:12:22.920 --> 01:12:25.000
my 13-year-old son thinks the hospital

1694
01:12:25.000 --> 01:12:27.340
that Jim and Pam go to is the Scrubs Hospital.

1695
01:12:27.340 --> 01:12:28.260
Is he right?

1696
01:12:28.260 --> 01:12:29.600
He's a huge Office fan.

1697
01:12:30.060 --> 01:12:31.100
And Sam O.

1698
01:12:31.300 --> 01:12:32.940
from Milwaukee, Wisconsin said,

1699
01:12:33.360 --> 01:12:34.500
at the end of this episode,

1700
01:12:34.620 --> 01:12:37.720
you guys are clearly in the hospital from Scrubs.

1701
01:12:37.940 --> 01:12:40.060
Do you remember anything about working there?

1702
01:12:40.060 --> 01:12:42.420
Was the cast of the other show around at all?

1703
01:12:42.600 --> 01:12:43.840
Well, I tell you what,

1704
01:12:44.000 --> 01:12:45.420
Christy, your son is right.

1705
01:12:46.020 --> 01:12:47.260
Sam, you are right.

1706
01:12:47.640 --> 01:12:52.060
This was the hospital that they used on Scrubs.

1707
01:12:52.580 --> 01:12:54.260
It is a former hospital.

1708
01:12:54.260 --> 01:12:55.680
It's not even around anymore.

1709
01:12:55.880 --> 01:12:56.720
They've torn it down.

1710
01:12:56.860 --> 01:12:59.460
But at the time, it was an abandoned hospital.

1711
01:12:59.660 --> 01:13:02.400
It was the Riverside Community Hospital in Sherman Oaks.

1712
01:13:02.640 --> 01:13:04.940
The Scrubs cast were not there that day,

1713
01:13:04.940 --> 01:13:07.880
but Randy told us that their production

1714
01:13:07.880 --> 01:13:09.880
graciously allowed us to use

1715
01:13:09.880 --> 01:13:11.720
some of their pre-dressed corridors

1716
01:13:11.720 --> 01:13:13.200
and examination rooMs.

1717
01:13:13.460 --> 01:13:14.980
And something I'll tell you

1718
01:13:14.980 --> 01:13:19.500
is that we shot all of this hospital stuff on Monday.

1719
01:13:19.500 --> 01:13:21.540
It was our very first day of shooting.

1720
01:13:21.660 --> 01:13:24.240
It was before we ever went out to the company picnic.

1721
01:13:24.560 --> 01:13:28.120
So all of that emotion was just day one.

1722
01:13:28.260 --> 01:13:28.700
Day one.

1723
01:13:28.880 --> 01:13:29.060
Wow.

1724
01:13:29.060 --> 01:13:30.700
We started with the cold open,

1725
01:13:30.700 --> 01:13:32.780
and then we relocated to the hospital.

1726
01:13:33.160 --> 01:13:37.000
And Jenny recalled that she was not allowed

1727
01:13:37.000 --> 01:13:38.640
to observe the hospital.

1728
01:13:38.900 --> 01:13:40.740
She knew that we were going to a hospital,

1729
01:13:40.740 --> 01:13:42.100
but she didn't know why.

1730
01:13:42.300 --> 01:13:44.700
And we'll tell you more about that in just a little bit.

1731
01:13:44.940 --> 01:13:47.080
I don't know how much longer Dwight can stall.

1732
01:13:47.300 --> 01:13:49.120
The corporate team is insisting

1733
01:13:49.120 --> 01:13:50.740
that Scranton put in their subs.

1734
01:13:50.940 --> 01:13:54.060
And Dwight is doing this really long roundabout thing

1735
01:13:54.060 --> 01:13:55.740
of like, well, how many people must get hurt

1736
01:13:55.740 --> 01:13:56.960
before a lesson is learned?

1737
01:13:56.960 --> 01:14:01.600
One, two, three, four.

1738
01:14:01.920 --> 01:14:04.220
He's doing a horrible job of stalling.

1739
01:14:04.380 --> 01:14:06.520
But Jim is like, Dwight, keep stalling.

1740
01:14:06.640 --> 01:14:09.820
And then he gets called into the room where Pam is.

1741
01:14:10.020 --> 01:14:12.580
And they get some pretty big news.

1742
01:14:12.740 --> 01:14:14.260
But we can't hear it.

1743
01:14:14.500 --> 01:14:14.980
Nope.

1744
01:14:15.280 --> 01:14:16.940
But I think we know what it is.

1745
01:14:17.040 --> 01:14:17.480
Yes.

1746
01:14:17.860 --> 01:14:19.140
We got some mail.

1747
01:14:19.460 --> 01:14:21.440
A lot of people wanted to know,

1748
01:14:21.600 --> 01:14:24.300
why was this scene silent?

1749
01:14:25.400 --> 01:14:28.120
Obviously, they're being told that they're going to have a baby.

1750
01:14:28.340 --> 01:14:29.500
Why couldn't we hear it?

1751
01:14:30.120 --> 01:14:33.220
Well, this was partially inspired by the British show.

1752
01:14:33.420 --> 01:14:37.460
There is a scene in that series where Tim is going to tell Dawn

1753
01:14:37.460 --> 01:14:38.520
how he feels about her.

1754
01:14:38.680 --> 01:14:40.600
But first, he takes off his microphone.

1755
01:14:41.140 --> 01:14:46.480
And Jen and Paul thought that this made that moment even more intimate.

1756
01:14:47.060 --> 01:14:49.900
It's one of those things, kind of like the teapot note.

1757
01:14:49.900 --> 01:14:56.000
There's nothing that you could write that could ever meet people's expectations

1758
01:14:56.000 --> 01:14:58.060
of what it needed to be.

1759
01:14:58.200 --> 01:15:01.520
So if you leave it for people to fill in themselves,

1760
01:15:01.520 --> 01:15:03.620
it'll always be the perfect note.

1761
01:15:03.860 --> 01:15:04.560
I agree.

1762
01:15:04.560 --> 01:15:06.980
And I feel like Randall Einhorn shared with us that

1763
01:15:06.980 --> 01:15:09.040
the further you were away from a moment,

1764
01:15:09.220 --> 01:15:11.200
the more intimate it feels to watch.

1765
01:15:11.520 --> 01:15:11.840
Yeah.

1766
01:15:12.100 --> 01:15:14.920
And so removing the sound makes you pretty far away.

1767
01:15:15.260 --> 01:15:15.560
Yeah.

1768
01:15:15.560 --> 01:15:19.520
Well, this idea was something we had been toying with for a long time.

1769
01:15:19.720 --> 01:15:23.060
On casino night, there was a whole conversation about whether or not

1770
01:15:23.060 --> 01:15:28.100
we should hear Jim tell Pam that he has feelings for her out in the parking lot.

1771
01:15:28.200 --> 01:15:31.400
We ultimately decided to keep the audio for that.

1772
01:15:31.620 --> 01:15:35.340
But we're going to do this again when Pam says goodbye to Michael.

1773
01:15:35.780 --> 01:15:40.120
Every once in a while, it was a trick we could use because we were a documentary.

1774
01:15:40.160 --> 01:15:43.600
We could pull the sound and make a really impactful moment.

1775
01:15:43.600 --> 01:15:47.020
So Jim is going to run into the hallway now.

1776
01:15:47.220 --> 01:15:51.480
He's going to call Dwight and he's going to say, send in the subs.

1777
01:15:51.820 --> 01:15:52.720
We got mail.

1778
01:15:53.680 --> 01:15:54.200
Annette E.

1779
01:15:54.460 --> 01:15:55.560
from Minnesota said,

